SQL> -- INTENT:
SQL> -- Purpose: Tear down the entire ROAD framework scaffold from an application schema.
SQL> -- Approach: Run the drop/ chain in reverse dependency order (ORDS modules first,
SQL> --   tables last).
SQL> -- Reason: Clean-slate rebuild during development.
SQL> -- Expected objects: ALL scaffold objects REMOVED -
SQL> --   ORDS modules: health, auth, session, ui
SQL> --   UI_ASSETS_API, HEALTH_API, JWT_SCAFFOLD_AUTH_API, SESSION_API
SQL> --   UI_ASSETS, JWT_SCAFFOLD_CONFIG (and all data in them)
SQL> -- Risk: HIGH - DESTRUCTIVE AND IRREVERSIBLE. Drops tables and every row they contain,
SQL> --   including uploaded UI assets and JWT signing key material. There is no backup step
SQL> --   in this script. Never run against test or prod without an explicit, separately
SQL> --   confirmed decision; prod additionally requires ALLOW_PROD_SQL=yes.
SQL> -- Prior history checked: Confirm the target environment in db-history before running,
SQL> --   and confirm the connection is the one you think it is.
