SQL> prompt === drop composition guard assertions (spec patch 07) ===
=== drop composition guard assertions (spec patch 07) ===
SQL> 
SQL> -- Must drop BEFORE the tables they depend on -- deploy/drop/00_full.sql runs this file first, for
SQL> -- exactly that reason (spec-patch-07 section 5.4). A teardown that leaves an assertion behind
SQL> -- blocks the rebuild, the same failure mode DROP ANY CONTEXT was added for in patch 06.
SQL> --
SQL> -- ORA-13650 ("the specified object does not exist for this execution") is what 26ai raises for
SQL> -- DROP ASSERTION on a name that isn't there -- confirmed empirically, not assumed, since assertion
SQL> -- error codes are undocumented territory for this project. Tolerated so teardown completes on a
SQL> -- schema where these were never created.
